# spectate_fight (spectator mode, 2026-11-07). No player and no orders: two NPC squads on the open ground past the Hub's Bar whose
# factions make them enemies (Berserkers -> Bloodraiders is a listed -100, and the Bloodraiders' default relation is -100), so the
# sensor rule (a relation at or below -30) starts the fight on sight. The bodies are the squad templates' own member records (Blood
# Raider 16863, Berserker 42259), as the original spawns them: unarmed, so nobody stands off with a crossbow (v3; the Dust bandit
# record these used to be carries a crossbow and one of eight held its ground at 220 u, kenshi-k16.6.95).
# Staging (kenshi-k16.6.124, rwh.91 section 2 / rwh.102): the facings are the original's generated set, not one yaw per squad, and `sheathed=1` puts each
# body's weapon on the back as the original's spawn does (the draw is the plan's task 6, when a member gets a target).
# The server places the world from the file (SCENARIO_IMPORT.md "Rule"); an empty player faction is allowed (scenario::apply makes none).
KSCEN 2
scenario title=Two%20squads%20on%20the%20open%20ground setup=No%20player%20and%20no%20orders%3A%20a%20Blood%20raider%20patrol%20of%20four%20east%20of%20the%20Hub%27s%20Bar%2C%20a%20Berserker%20patrol%20of%20four%20226%20u%20north%20of%20it%2C%20mutually%20hostile. look_for=The%20two%20patrols%20see%20each%20other%20and%20fight%20within%20a%20minute%20of%20game%20time%2C%20with%20nobody%20ordered.%20Do%20they%20close%20in%20or%20stand%20apart%3F%20Who%20goes%20down%20first%3F%20Do%20squadmates%20join%20a%20fight%20in%20progress%3F bead=kenshi-h2v.2 metrics=fight_s,bodies_down
